- **R44.** Keep the SSDP discovery and DLNA SOAP stack (pure Rust `ureq` + UDP) unchanged except: bind to the Wi-Fi interface address (the existing private-LAN selection logic works) and keep cast control in the foreground or in the mediaPlayback service to respect Android 15+ background network restrictions. Keep the token-authenticated LAN HTTP range server for casting to TV browsers; document that long casts require the app to stay in the foreground or in the foreground service. Keep all security limits: RFC-1918-only targets, 256 KB XML cap, constant-time token comparison, eight-connection cap.
- **R45.** Replace `aaz_cast_open_windows_cast` (opens Windows settings) with Android's system output switcher via `MediaRouter`, or hide that button on Android if MediaRouter integration is deferred. Record the choice in the architecture record.
- **R46.** **Verify** end-to-end casting to at least one real DLNA TV/renderer and one phone browser on the same Wi-Fi, including VTT subtitle timing sync and the `?token=...&t=...` URL joining already covered by tests.
- **R47.** Final permission audit (each justified in the PR): `INTERNET`, `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE`, `CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE`, `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO` + `READ_MEDIA_VIDEO` (API 33+, device-media flows only), `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` with `maxSdkVersion="32"`, `WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` with `maxSdkVersion="28"` (R16 snapshots on API 24-28), `FOREGROUND_SERVICE` (install-time, targeting 28+), `FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK` (install-time, when targeting 34+), `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` (33+, the only runtime-gated one of this group), `WAKE_LOCK`, and `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES` for the self-update track (D9). Network security: keep cleartext disabled except the localhost/LAN cast server; if a `networkSecurityConfig` is needed, scope it to private ranges and document it. Backup rules: keep `android:allowBackup` with rules excluding cast session tokens.
- **R48.** Distribution (D9): the shipping track is the direct signed APK from GitHub Releases. Reuse the existing updater architecture for APKs: version check against GitHub Releases, download with the same caps (150 MB, atomic `.part`, HTTPS allowlist, SHA-256 from `SHA256SUMS.txt`, Minisign trusted-comment binding, all portable Rust), then install via `PackageInstaller` with `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES` and the user's runtime "install unknown apps" consent. The optional Play Store track (AAB via `tauri android build --aab`, Play App Signing, self-updater feature-flagged off per Play policy) is documented but out of scope for these phases.
- **R49.** Signing (D5). Direct distribution has no upload-key layer: the release keystore created here IS the app signing key. The upload-key/app-signing-key split exists only under Play App Signing on the Play track (out of scope, D9), where Google manages the app signing key and the developer holds an upload key. Generate a new keystore with `keytool` (RSA 2048, validity 10000 days), store `keystore.properties` in `gen/android/` (gitignored), and wire the release `signingConfigs` in `app/build.gradle.kts` exactly as the official Tauri Android signing guide shows. Key material never enters the repo, this prompt, or any output: CI holds `ANDROID_KEY_BASE64`, `ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS`, and `ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD` as secrets, base64-decoded at build time per the guide's workflow snippet. Back the keystore up offline and treat that backup as a release requirement: on the direct track, update key continuity is intended — the signing certificate is the update identity, so losing this key breaks updates for existing installs on that track (a future Play track under Play App Signing would have its own key-recovery story). Debug builds use the debug key; verify release builds with `apksigner verify`; record the release certificate SHA-256 fingerprint in the README so users can confirm authenticity.
- **R50.** Release CI: extend `.github/workflows/release.yml` with an Android matrix job building the signed release APK for all four ABIs, extending `SHA256SUMS.txt` to the APK, and keeping the fail-closed signing gate (missing secrets means no stable release) consistent with the Windows flow. Ship a universal APK first; `--split-per-abi` optional later; report the release APK size.
