## 9. Testing and acceptance

- **T1. Build:** `tauri android build --apk` produces a working debug APK in Phase 1 and signed release APKs (all four ABIs with `--split-per-abi`, or universal) in Phase 4; `apksigner verify` passes on release.
- **T2. Boot:** cold start to interactive in 2.5 s or less on a mid-range device; record the device and measurement.
- **T3. Regression:** all 27 JS test groups, `cargo test`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` pass; the Windows CI stays green on the same commit.
- **T4. Media matrix:** on API 26, 29, 33, and 35 emulators plus one physical device, play: MP4/H.264+AAC, MP4/HEVC, MKV/VP9+Opus, MKV/H.264+AC-3 (expect audio if the V2 FFmpeg extension shipped; otherwise silent audio plus the user notice — record which), WebM, MP3, FLAC, WAV, M4A, OGG, Opus. Record pass/fail per device.
- **T5. Storage:** an SAF folder with Arabic filenames and 500 or more files scans in under 5 s; persisted permissions survive reboot; a revoked permission shows the designed error state.
- **T6. Subtitles:** auto-match finds an Arabic-tagged `.srt` beside a video inside an SAF tree; the style editor round-trips all 14 fields; 0.25 s shift works; cast VTT timing stays synced.
- **T7. Background:** audio keeps playing for 30 minutes with the screen off and the app backgrounded on a physical device; video keeps playing as background audio; lock-screen and notification controls work; a phone call pauses and resumes playback.
- **T8. Cast:** DLNA renderer and phone-browser playback with subtitles; multicast lock acquired and released (log evidence); no crash when Wi-Fi toggles mid-cast.
- **T9. Process death:** swipe away or kill during playback, relaunch, and the queue, position, volume, theme, and language are restored.
- **T10. UI:** 390 px and tablet screenshots for every enabled theme in Arabic and English; no clipped text; 44 dp targets verified in Layout Inspector; RTL mirror audit.
- **T11. Battery:** 60 minutes of screen-off audio playback costs 8% battery or less on the physical device; record the level.
- **T12. Privacy hygiene:** a network inspector shows zero third-party hosts during full use (cast and update-check excluded and user-initiated); no debug symbols in release; R8/ProGuard config verified.

## 10. Final directive

Start Phase 1 now. The decisions in Part 1 are final: same repository, shared web UI with a native Media3 playback core behind a Kotlin Tauri plugin, phones and tablets, minSdk 24 with runtime gates, green theme first, manual picking first plus MediaStore scan in Phase 2, open-from-other-apps in Phase 1, direct signed APK distribution, fully offline with no accounts or tracking. Execute one phase at a time; a phase closes only when its gate passes with recorded evidence. If runtime evidence contradicts a decision mid-flight (for example T7 failing), apply the documented fallback for that decision and record it in the architecture record instead of silently re-scoping.

## 11. Risks, unknowns, and honesty rules

- `aazmedia://` custom protocol on Android WebView: believed supported in current Tauri v2 (the earlier Android custom-protocol crash was fixed upstream), but V1 must prove Range behavior before web-loaded resources rely on it; playback itself never depends on it (R13).
- Native video surface layering with the Tauri WebView (z-order, resize, rotation): V2 must prove it on the test matrix before Phase 1 builds on it; the D2 surface fallback covers failure without changing playback ownership.
- Platform decoder variance across OEMs (especially HEVC, AV1, AC-3): documentation lists a baseline and devices differ; the T4 probe matrix is the source of truth, never the documentation. The Media3 FFmpeg extension must be built manually; if its build or licensing review fails, the affected formats fall back to the R15 notice.
- WebView video fullscreen and PiP behavior varies by WebView version; R18 and R39 carry fallbacks and runtime gates for the D2 fallback paths.
- SAF tree traversal is slower than `std::fs`; keep the 25,000-entry scan cap from desktop and show progress UI on large trees.
- Android 15+ background network limits make casting foreground/service-bound by design; never promise background casting.
- Where a requirement conflicts with Play policy (the `READ_MEDIA_*` restricted use cases, `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES`), prefer SAF and photo-picker flows and cite the policy.
- Consult first: v2.tauri.app (prerequisites, Android signing, Google Play distribution, dialog plugin, mobile plugin development), developer.android.com (media formats, scoped storage and MediaStore, foreground services, media sessions, edge-to-edge), and MDN browser-compat data for WebView API gaps. Cite what you verified, when, and on which device and API level.
- Final rule: never report a feature as working without a device or emulator artifact (screenshot, screen recording, or log excerpt) attached to the acceptance matrix.